s="xafu7qg"><img class="fill-img" src="/assets/img/loose-tube-outdoor-fiber-optic-cable-on-a-d1ad7f.png" srcset="/assets/img/loose-tube-outdoor-fiber-optic-cable-on-a-d1ad7f-512w.webp 512w, /assets/img/loose-tube-outdoor-fiber-optic-cable-on-a-d1ad7f-1024w.webp 1024w, /assets/img/loose-tube-outdoor-fiber-optic-cable-on-a-d1ad7f.png 1920w" sizes="(min-width: 810px) and (max-width: 1199.98px) 100vw, (max-width: 809.98px) 100vw, 100vw" width="1920" height="1080" alt="Loose-tube outdoor fiber optic cable on a reel" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/></div><div class="section-introduction xpfskxn"><h2 class="xhz5zt5">What it is</h2><p class="xuvmvsv">Loose-tube stranded cable is the workhorse of outside plant. Fibers sit loose in gel-filled tubes stranded around a central member, giving the cable the mechanical and environmental protection outdoor routes demand: duct, aerial or direct-burial. Its all-dielectric, non-metallic construction removes the need for bonding and grounding.</p></div><div class="specification-table xcqzusx fb"><div class="construction-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Construction</p><p class="xcclquv">Stranded loose-tube, gel-filled</p></div><div class="strength-member-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Strength member</p><p class="xcclquv">Non-metallic (all-dielectric)</p></div><div class="fibre-type-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Fiber type</p><p class="xcclquv">G.652D single-mode (G.657A1 available)</p></div><div class="fibre-counts-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Fiber counts</p><p class="xcclquv">12F, 24F, 48F, 72F, 96F, 144F, 288F, 432F, 576F, 864F</p></div><div class="sheath-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Sheath</p><p class="xcclquv">PE (double-jacket / armoured options)</p></div><div class="deployment-row xcj10xy fb"><p class="xbslay4">Deployment</p><p class="xcclquv">Duct · aerial lashed · direct-burial</p></div><div class="standards-row xr2tetp"><p class="xbslay4">Standards</p><p class="xcclquv">build-to-order to your route specification</p></div></div></section><section class="fibre-count-range xqjs4fo"><h2 class="xqmzbdo">From access to backbone</h2><p class="xbt6gdt">Low counts for distribution and last-mile, high counts for metro and long-haul backbone. Specified per route and supplied to order.</p><div class="count-rail xhrktuh"><div class="12f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">12F</p></div><div class="24f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">24F</p></div><div class="48f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">48F</p></div><div class="72f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">72F</p></div><div class="96f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">96F</p></div><div class="144f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">144F</p></div><div class="288f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">288F</p></div><div class="432f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">432F</p></div><div class="576f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">576F</p></div><div class="864f xvahfb7"><p class="xzxqqpp">864F</p></div></div></section><div class="section-divider xbstc8l"><div class="x2h0iev"></div><div class="xqo6eaw"></div><div class="x2h0iev"></div></div><div class="individual-products xjpxpkl"><h3 class="xntyyys">Browse individual products</h3><div class="product-links xawjyfv">{products.filter((item) => item.data.category === "Outside Plant Loose Tube Cable").map((item) => (<a class="product-link xllccit fb" href={"/products/" + item.id}><p class="x6ieutw">{item.data.name}</p></a>))}</div></div><section class="where-it-s-used x6mc4fb"><div class="use-cases-introduction xn9jb0l"><h2 class="x2aydey">Where it’s used</h2><p class="xjuo1l3">We don't disclose client names, but here are a few examples of the work we've delivered.</p></div><div class="use-case-grid xadgwt5"><div class="open-access-ftth-card xvnp2zm fb"><div class="logo-slot xvreelm fb"><p class="x7dsupb">1</p></div><p class="xewtdrd">Open-access FTTH · California, Colorado, Minnesota: GCYFTY-144 loose-tube for multi-state open-access builds.</p></div><div class="national-broadband-card xvnp2zm fb"><div class="logo-slot xvreelm fb"><p class="x